GJClasses CHANGELOG
===================
v0.55.0    2026-10-18
- Added .github/dependabot.yml so Dependabot opens one grouped Composer
  update PR a month, with a 7-day cooldown, and turned on vulnerability
  alerts and automatic security fix PRs on GitHub. Consumers ignore
  this library's composer.lock, so a PR that only bumps the lock needs
  no release; one that changes a constraint in composer.json reaches
  them only with a new v0.N.0 tag
- Upgraded the dependencies that were pinned to old major versions,
  which forced every consumer onto Guzzle 6, firebase/php-jwt 4, and
  other releases with known vulnerabilities (19 Dependabot alerts,
  including one critical). The new constraints are auth0/auth0-php
  ^8.17, irazasyed/telegram-bot-sdk ^3.16, donatj/pushover ^3.2, and
  phpmailer/phpmailer ^6.0 || ^7.0, and the lock file now has no
  known advisories
- Raised the minimum PHP version to 8.2, which auth0/auth0-php 8.17
  and later require
- Rewrote the Auth0 class for auth0-php 8: the config uses its
  camelCase keys, scope and audience are passed as arrays, and a new
  GJC_AUTH0_COOKIE_SECRET constant is required. queryUserInfo is on,
  so the user profile still comes from /userinfo as it did with
  auth0-php 5, not only from the ID token. login() and logout()
  now do the redirect themselves, since the SDK only returns the URL,
  and logout() uses the SDK's https logout link instead of building
  an http one. check() now exchanges the code on the callback page,
  which auth0-php 8 no longer does inside getUser(), so callback pages
  that call check() keep working. A stale, replayed, or failed
  callback now redirects to the login page instead of throwing, and
  the session cookies are marked Secure when the callback URL is https
- Kept Pushover's "Message Failed" behaviour: donatj/pushover 3 throws
  a ResponseException on failure instead of returning false, so the
  class now catches it
- Added GJC_AUTH0_COOKIE_SECRET to examples/auth0.php

